# Ocentra Games – Security Rules & Guarantees (MANDATORY)

> This document defines **security guarantees, threats, and invariants** for any system that:

> - Handles money
> - Interacts with Solana
> - Exposes HTTP / Web / RPC endpoints
>
> **Security failures are correctness failures.**
>
> No Solana basics, no hand-holding — this is written as if the adversary understands Web3 + infra.

---

## Document Purpose & Scope

This document defines **WHAT must never break** (security guarantees) and **WHAT threats exist** (threat model).

**This document does NOT define:**

- How to write tests (see `ocentra-test-rules.mdc`)
- Test tooling or CI mechanics (see `ocentra-security-guidelines.mdc`)
- Test quality standards (see `ocentra-test-rules.mdc` §0.2)

**Key Principle:**
> Security guarantees exist independently of tests; tests are only evidence of enforcement.

### Related Documents

- **Test writing standards**: `ocentra-test-rules.mdc` - How to write tests, test quality, proof standards
- **Test tooling & CI setup**: `ocentra-security-guidelines.mdc` - Required tools, CI pipeline, test categories overview
- **Security guarantees & rules** (this document): `ocentra-security-rules.mdc` - What must never break, numbered rules

### Document Structure

- **§0.1**: Security Guarantees (G1-G6) - Non-negotiable guarantees
- **§0.2**: Security Meta-Invariants - Things that must NEVER be true
- **§1-12**: Specific security test requirements (numbered rules)
- **§13**: Security Test Acceptance Checklist
- **§14**: Security Coverage Gate (mandatory test categories)
- **§15**: Advanced Security Testing Requirements (system-level)

All rules are numbered for violation reporting (e.g., "Violation 1.1.5", "Violation 15.4.1.3").

