## 1. CORS & Origin Security

### Rule 1.1: MUST HAVE TESTS FOR

- **Rule 1.1.1:** Missing `Origin` header
- **Rule 1.1.2:** Empty `Origin` header
- **Rule 1.1.3:** `null` origin
- **Rule 1.1.4:** Untrusted origin (explicit deny)
- **Rule 1.1.5:** Subdomain takeover origin
- **Rule 1.1.6:** Scheme mismatch (`http` vs `https`)
- **Rule 1.1.7:** Port mismatch
- **Rule 1.1.8:** Mixed-case origin (`ExAmPlE.com`)
- **Rule 1.1.9:** Trailing dot origin (`example.com.`)
- **Rule 1.1.10:** IDN / punycode origin confusion
- **Rule 1.1.11:** IP-based origin (`http://127.0.0.1`)
- **Rule 1.1.12:** IPv6 origin
- **Rule 1.1.13:** Wildcard origin (`*`) with credentials
- **Rule 1.1.14:** Reflected origin without allowlist
- **Rule 1.1.15:** Cached preflight reused across origins
- **Rule 1.1.16:** Multiple `Origin` headers
- **Rule 1.1.17:** Origin vs `Host` mismatch
- **Rule 1.1.18:** Origin allowed but method disallowed
- **Rule 1.1.19:** Origin allowed but headers disallowed
- **Rule 1.1.20:** Origin allowlist tied to **environment**
- **Rule 1.1.21:** Mobile app WebView origins
- **Rule 1.1.22:** Deep-link origin spoofing
- **Rule 1.1.23:** Wallet-embedded browser quirks
- **Rule 1.1.24:** Preflight cache poisoning under concurrency

### Rule 1.2: MUST HAVE FUZZ TESTS FOR

- **Rule 1.2.1:** Origin string mutations
- **Rule 1.2.2:** Unicode homoglyphs
- **Rule 1.2.3:** Overlong origin strings
- **Rule 1.2.4:** Null byte injection
- **Rule 1.2.5:** Embedded credentials (`https://user@host`)
- **Rule 1.2.6:** Header folding / CRLF injection

**PASS CONDITION**

- Exact origin handling
- No `*` in credentialed responses
- CORS misconfiguration = security bug, not config detail

> Web3 wallets are hostile browsers.

